+# The Daily Grind
+
+Marketing site for The Daily Grind coffee company, served by a small dependency-light Node server.
+
+```sh
+pnpm install
+pnpm start          # http://localhost:11222
+pnpm test           # node:test suites in test/
+```
+
+## Rewards sign-up with browser-assisted e-mail verification
+
+The homepage has a **Daily Grind Rewards** sign-up form that proves the customer owns
+their e-mail address *without* sending a one-time passcode or magic link. It uses the
+browser's Email Verification API / Email Verification Protocol (EVP):
+
+1. `GET /` renders the form with a hidden
+   `<input name="token" autocomplete="email-verification-token" nonce="…">` next to the
+   `autocomplete="email"` input. The nonce (256 bits) is minted per render, kept in
+   server-side session state keyed by the `dg_sid` HttpOnly cookie, and the page is sent
+   with `Cache-Control: no-store`.
+2. When the user picks an address they are signed in to, the browser asks the e-mail
+   provider for an Email Verification Token (an SD-JWT), binds it to this origin and nonce
+   in a Key-Binding JWT, fills the hidden input and submits.
+3. `POST /api/rewards/verify-email` consumes the nonce (read + delete) and verifies the
+   whole chain in `lib/email-verification.mjs` with `@sd-jwt/core` and `jose`:
+   e-mail claim match, DNS delegation (`_email-verification.<domain>` TXT), issuer
+   discovery (`/.well-known/email-verification`) + JWKS, EVT signature, KB-JWT signature,
+   nonce, audience, freshness, `sd_hash`.
+4. On success the account is created already verified (`201`, `status: "verified"`).
+   If the token is empty (unsupported browser, signed-out user, non-participating
+   domain) or fails any check, the server falls back to the classic confirmation
+   e-mail path (`202`, `status: "pending_email"`) and never blocks sign-up.
+
+The form works without JavaScript (plain POST → HTML page); with JavaScript it posts via
+`fetch`, shows the outcome inline and re-arms the hidden input with the replacement nonce
+returned on error responses.
+
+### Configuration
+
+| Variable | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `PORT` | Listen port (default `11222`). |
+| `RP_ORIGIN` | Public origin used as the expected KB-JWT audience, e.g. `https://dailygrind.example`. Defaults to the request origin (honours `X-Forwarded-Proto/Host`). |
+| `ORIGIN_TRIAL_TOKEN` | Chrome Origin Trial token for the Email Verification API, emitted as the `Origin-Trial` response header. Without it the browser ignores the hidden input and every sign-up takes the e-mail fallback. |
+| `INSECURE_COOKIES=1` | Drop the `Secure` cookie flag for plain-http development on a non-localhost host. |
+
+### Not wired up (intentionally stubbed)
+
+* Accounts and nonces live in memory (`Map`). Use Redis or a database for multi-instance deployments.
+* `sendTraditionalVerificationEmail()` logs the confirmation code instead of sending mail.
